  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-4},
  abstract={This paper presents the design aspects and realization of a dual circularly polarized aperture coupled antenna array for Launch Vehicle telemetry reception. An antenna array tile consists of $4 \times 4$ aperture coupled patch antenna elements, $4 \times 4$ quadrature hybrids and RHCP/LHCP feed network is realized using Rogers RO4003 substrate in a multi-layer configuration. Rohacell foam material, with a dielectric constant of 1.06 and a thickness of 5 mm, is used between the patch array and the quadrature hybrid feed network to reduce weight and enhance impedance bandwidth. The antenna array has a 2:1 VSWR bandwidth of 11.5% centered at 2.25 GHz and gain of 16 dBi throughout the required telemetry band of 2.2 GHz to 2.3 GHz. Overall dimension of the antenna array tile is 300mm × 300mm × 9mm.},
