  title={Receding Horizon Planning and Guidance for Powered Landing Using Thrust Level-wise Release and Apparent Acceleration Compensation}, 
  year={2022},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1288-1292},
  abstract={The guidance problem of powered landing is investigated in this paper considering modeling deviation and wind interference. Firstly a receding horizon guidance method for rocket powered landing based on online convex optimization is investigated. Considering the insufficient control capability of rocket engine, we propose the strategy that the upper bound of thrust is released step by step during the ending phase of landing. Meanwhile, to reduce the influence of disturbance and modeling error, online planed thrust command is compensated by apparent acceleration in each guidance period, which promotes recursive feasibility of the planning algorithm. Finally, mathematical simulation results illustrate the effectiveness and performance of the planning algorithm and compensation strategy.},
  keywords={Rockets;Upper bound;Simulation;Interference;Numerical simulation;Robustness;Convex functions;powered landing;trajectory planning;convex optimization;receding horizon;successive convexification},
  doi={10.1109/ICUS55513.2022.9987079},
