  abstract={THE LAST TIME an American-built spacecraft delivered astronauts to the International Space Station was July 2011. The following month, the Space Shuttle fleet was officially retired and the orbiters now reside in museums across the US. Since then, the only option for Nasa has been to fly its astronauts on the Russian Soyuz at a cost of some $70m per round trip.},
  keywords={},
