  title={Distributed Data Acquisition and Control System for Rocket Engine Static-Fire Test Stands}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-12},
  abstract={A modular, Ethernet-based control and data acquisition architecture for rocket engine test stands is presented. Each hardware module combines a universal controller Core board, providing Power over Ethernet (PoE) and IEEE 1588 Precision Time Protocol (PTP) synchronization-with a swappable I/O Slave board tailored to specific sensors or actuators. A centralized server implements a software defined Layer 2 overlay that maintains time alignment, enforces quality-of-service, and prioritizes critical commands in commodity networks. The design emphasizes fault isolation and rapid reconfiguration: modules can be added, replaced, or upgraded without system-wide changes. Compared to monolithic controllers, the approach offers (i) plug-and-play scalability, (ii) tight network-level timing across distributed devices, and (iii) robust performance under high telemetry load. The architecture extends to ground systems such as launch-pad automation and propellant handling. Validation will use small-scale static-fire tests of a 4 kN liquid-propellant motor. The paper details the design, architecture and implementation of the presented system.},
