  pages={1-4},
  abstract={The paper presents the results of experimental studies of the electrodynamic characteristics of ceramic materials obtained on the basis of the target phases of the RO - Al2O3 - SiO2 (RO - SrO, BaO, ZnO). The main attention is paid to the analysis of the transmission, reflection and absorption coefficients for slawsonite, celsian, celsian-slawsonite and slawsonite-willemite ceramics in the frequency range of 26.5…38 GHz. It is established that the studied ceramic materials demonstrate the stability of electrodynamic parameters in a given frequency range and provide the required level of radio transparency. The possibilities of using the studied materials in the designs of aviation and rocket technology in the manufacture of individual structural and protective elements are assessed. The feasibility of using heterophase ceramics of slawsonite-willemite composition for the manufacture of products with optimal dielectric properties, increased heat resistance and operating temperature up to 1100 °C is established. The results obtained can be used in the development of new types of radio-transparent protective structures for avionics.},
